"""
================================================================================
MASTER CLOCK = (VIDEO trimmed & re-zero) == (FIBER trimmed & re-zero)
MedPC is corrected INTO this master clock.

NEW ALIGNMENT PLAN (moderate anti-overfit)
------------------------------------------
1) Master clock:
   - Drop first TRIM_START_SEC from BOTH video and fiber, then re-zero => t_master=0.
2) Manual anchors:
   - You annotated on ORIGINAL video timeline => subtract TRIM_START_SEC => master manual times.
3) MedPC:
   - Raw ticks -> seconds, cluster.
   - Build an "event lattice" = candidate matrix (anchor x medpc candidates) using affine corridor.
4) Alignment:
   A) Coarse affine (a,b) by grid search + DP monotonic match (skip allowed).
   B) Build candidate matrix under corridor W_CAND (not too tight).
   C) Feature-aware DP: match cost = |time error| + lambda_noise * noise_penalty(medpc_event)
      + skip penalty (moderate).
   D) Refit affine from matched pairs with mild ridge to prevent overfitting:
      - pull 'a' toward 1.0 softly
      - pull 'b' toward clock prior softly
      - 1 iteration is enough.
5) Fiber peri-event:
   - Use corrected MedPC event times in master directly (no fiber warping).
6) VFR-safe clips:
   - Convert master time -> trimmed frame idx -> original frame idx.

================================================================================
"""

